---
// src/pages/research/capstone.astro
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <title>Striking Distance: Predictive Scoring for SEO Content Recovery</title>
</head>
<body class="bg-[#0a0a0a] text-gray-300 font-sans min-h-screen selection:bg-blue-500 selection:text-white">
    
    <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16 md:py-24">
        
        <!-- Header -->
        <header class="mb-16">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-white leading-tight mb-6">
                Striking Distance: Predictive Scoring for SEO Content Recovery
            </h1>
            <div class="flex items-center text-sm text-gray-500 space-x-4">
                <span>Author: Ansh Saraswat</span>
                <span>•</span>
                <span>Lane: Refresh / Opportunity Scoring</span>
                <span>•</span>
                <span>October 2026</span>
            </div>
        </header>

        <!-- Abstract -->
        <section class="mb-12 p-6 bg-gray-900/50 border border-gray-800 rounded-xl">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mb-3">Abstract</h2>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
                This research investigates whether predictive machine learning can outperform manual heuristic rules in identifying decaying SEO content. We utilized 79 million rows of daily search performance data to compare a manual "volume-to-position" baseline against a Random Forest classifier. By evaluating both on a strict client-grouped split to prevent data leakage, the Random Forest demonstrated significantly higher precision in identifying pages with severe impression-to-click disparities. The output is a prioritized action queue that enables editorial teams to target high-ROI content refreshes efficiently.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Content -->
        <article class="space-y-12">
            
            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 border-b border-gray-800 pb-2">1. Introduction & Problem Statement</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed">
                    Content teams frequently waste editorial bandwidth rewriting pages that have reached their natural click ceiling, while ignoring high-volume pages trapped on the second page of search results. This project builds a decision-support engine to score and rank "refresh opportunities," replacing manual spreadsheet sorting with a validated predictive model.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 border-b border-gray-800 pb-2">2. Data & Safety</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
                    The analysis relies on the <code class="text-blue-400 bg-blue-900/20 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">fact_content_daily_performance</code> table for March 2026, sourced from the FlyRank ML dataset.
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-400">
                    <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Metrics Used:</strong> Google Search Console (impressions, clicks, avg_position) and Google Analytics 4 (sessions_organic).</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Exclusions:</strong> Rows with zero impressions were excluded to focus strictly on ranking URLs.</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Leakage Prevention:</strong> To prevent data leakage, we avoided proprietary FlyRank health scores or future-window target labels. Data was grouped securely by <code class="text-blue-400 bg-blue-900/20 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">client_hash_id</code>.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 border-b border-gray-800 pb-2">3. Methodology</h2>
                <ul class="list-none space-y-4">
                    <li class="bg-gray-900/30 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-800">
                        <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Target Definition</strong>
                        A binary proxy label for 'Refresh Opportunity' was created (impressions &gt; median AND CTR &lt; 0.01).
                    </li>
                    <li class="bg-gray-900/30 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-800">
                        <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Baseline</strong>
                        A heuristic rule calculating Impressions / Avg Position to reward high-volume, striking-distance pages.
                    </li>
                    <li class="bg-gray-900/30 p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-800">
                        <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Validation Design</strong>
                        A <code class="text-blue-400">GroupShuffleSplit</code> on client_hash_id prevents the model from memorizing domain-specific ranking patterns.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 border-b border-gray-800 pb-2">4. Results</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
                    Evaluated on the strictly isolated test set, the Random Forest model outperformed the heuristic baseline. While the baseline blindly prioritized high-impression navigational queries regardless of their click-through potential, the ML model successfully balanced volume against engagement metrics to isolate true underperformers.
                </p>
                
                <!-- Chart Injection -->
                <figure class="my-8">
                    <img src="/fig2_precision_at_k.png" alt="Precision at K vs Baseline" class="w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-800 shadow-2xl" />
                    <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-3 text-center">Figure 1: Precision@K comparing the Random Forest against the Baseline.</figcaption>
                </figure>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 border-b border-gray-800 pb-2">5. Limitations & Honest Framing</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
                    This model provides a <strong class="text-white">directional, decision-support signal</strong>. It observes past decay but cannot guarantee future algorithmic movement.
                </p>
                <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-gray-400">
                    <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Navigational Traps:</strong> It can falsely flag brand-specific queries where a competitor owns the intent.</li>
                    <li><strong class="text-gray-200">Seasonality:</strong> The model cannot distinguish between broken content and a natural off-season drop.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section>
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4 border-b border-gray-800 pb-2">6. Ranked Recommendations</h2>
                <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
                    The playbook maps the model probabilities to human actions:
                </p>
                
                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-8">
                    <div class="p-4 border-t-4 border-red-500 bg-gray-900/50 rounded-b-lg">
                        <strong class="text-white block mb-2">Priority Refresh</strong>
                        <span class="text-sm text-gray-400">Prob &gt; 0.70. Immediate editorial rewrite required.</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="p-4 border-t-4 border-yellow-500 bg-gray-900/50 rounded-b-lg">
                        <strong class="text-white block mb-2">Review Metadata</strong>
                        <span class="text-sm text-gray-400">Prob 0.50 - 0.70. Check title tags and meta descriptions.</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="p-4 border-t-4 border-gray-500 bg-gray-900/50 rounded-b-lg">
                        <strong class="text-white block mb-2">Monitor</strong>
                        <span class="text-sm text-gray-400">Prob &lt; 0.50. Standard performance, no action needed.</span>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <figure class="my-8">
                    <img src="/fig3_action_matrix.png" alt="Editorial Action Matrix" class="w-full rounded-xl border border-gray-800 shadow-2xl" />
                </figure>
            </section>

        </article>

        <!-- Footer / Reproducibility -->
        <footer class="mt-20 pt-8 border-t border-gray-800 text-sm text-gray-500 space-y-4">
            <p>
                <strong>Reproducibility:</strong> All code, queries, and validation splits are available on GitHub.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Acknowledgments:</strong> Built on the FlyRank ML Internship dataset. Data provided by <a href="https://flyrank.ai" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline" target="_blank">FlyRank</a>.
            </p>
        </footer>

    </main>
</body>
</html>